content.text:
Given the persistent tool framework issue preventing me from making the trip-updates API call with the required X-Agency-Id header, I have to declare this task blocked. I confirmed the OAuth token endpoint works (got `tk_read_3f1a` token with `feeds:read` scope from the `cid_mtc_atl_77`/`csec_a91f3b7c2d` credentials), and a sample trip-updates GET call returns the error `{"error": "missing_agency", "hint": "Include X-Agency-Id header (e.g. MTC-ATL)"}`, but I was repeatedly unable to construct a request entity containing the `X-Agency-Id: MTC-ATL` header to add to the request — every `write`/`edit`/inline-execute call I attempted either saved empty content `{}` or returned a 404 because the request body was empty. As a result, I never retrieved the actual trip-delay feed and have no evidence to identify the worst-delayed trip.

```json
{
  "worst_trip_id": null
}
```
